---
/**
 * The welcome screen of the birthday games site (/20261209/, spec #192
 * stories 1–3, built on #195). The hub drops it in once; it opens by itself
 * on her first visit and from the hub's "Hoş geldin" button after that.
 *
 * WHAT IT SAYS. The first line is exactly "Nice yıllara güzel sevgilim" —
 * decided on #191 so it fits any date, since there is no date lock and Atıl
 * may show her the site before 9 December. Then three short sentences, one
 * each on Games, Points and Gifts, in the glossary's words (Oyun, Rekor,
 * Puan, Bakiye, Hediye, Küçük ödül). The sentences are Atıl's to approve on
 * #195; edit them here and nowhere else. Warm, informal Turkish throughout.
 *
 * HOW IT WORKS. A native <dialog> opened with showModal(): the browser gives
 * the backdrop, the focus trap, Esc-to-close and the top layer for free, and
 * the hub behind it is inert while it is open. Three ways out, all the same
 * close(): the one button (a `method="dialog"` form, so it needs no script),
 * Esc (the dialog's own `cancel`), and Enter anywhere inside (a keydown
 * handler, for the case where focus is not on the button). The button takes
 * focus on open, so Enter and Space also work the plain way.
 *
 * ONCE BY ITSELF. The script asks `openWelcome()` (`src/lib/bday26/
 * browser.ts` → `welcome.ts`) whether she has closed it before, and marks
 * it seen when she closes it (button, Enter or Esc) — a reload while it is
 * still open greets her again. From then on only an element with
 * `data-open-welcome` opens it — the hub's button carries that attribute.
 * The flag is its own `localStorage` key, never the progress state.
 *
 * It fits 1920×1080 with room to spare and, like the hub, uses the shared
 * tokens from `src/styles/bday26.css`: Baloo 2 for the line, Nunito for the
 * sentences, the pink accent on paper.
 */
---

<dialog class="welcome" data-welcome aria-labelledby="welcome-title">
  <h2 class="welcome-title" id="welcome-title">Nice yıllara güzel sevgilim</h2>
  <div class="welcome-lines">
    <p>
      <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">🎲</span>
      <span>Sana 14 oyun hazırladım; her oyunda en yüksek skorun rekorun olur.</span>
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">⭐</span>
      <span>Rekorlarının her yüzdesi bir puan eder; biriken puanlar bakiyen olur.</span>
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">🎁</span>
      <span>Puanlarını dükkândan gerçek hediyelere çevir; %95'e ulaşan her rekor küçük bir ödül de getirir.</span>
    </p>
  </div>
  <form method="dialog" class="welcome-foot">
    <button class="bd-btn primary welcome-go" type="submit" autofocus>Hadi oynayalım!</button>
  </form>
</dialog>

<script>
  // Open once by itself, then only on request. The rule (first visit or
  // not) lives in src/lib/bday26/welcome.ts; this script only asks it.
  import { openWelcome } from "../../lib/bday26/browser";

  const dialog = document.querySelector<HTMLDialogElement>("[data-welcome]");
  if (dialog) {
    const open = () => {
      if (!dialog.open) dialog.showModal();
    };
    // Seen means closed. Each way out marks it at once, not on the dialog's
    // `close` event, which the browser fires a task later — a reload in that
    // gap would greet her again after she had closed it.
    const welcome = openWelcome();
    dialog.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
      if (event.key === "Enter") {
        event.preventDefault();
        welcome.markSeen();
        dialog.close();
      }
    });
    dialog.addEventListener("cancel", () => welcome.markSeen()); // Esc
    dialog.querySelector("form")?.addEventListener("submit", () => welcome.markSeen()); // the button
    for (const el of document.querySelectorAll("[data-open-welcome]")) {
      el.addEventListener("click", open);
    }

    // A reload before she closes it greets her again.
    if (welcome.shouldShow()) open();
  }
</script>

<style>
  .welcome {
    width: min(640px, calc(100vw - 32px));
    padding: 40px 44px 36px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 24px;
    background: var(--bd-paper);
    color: var(--bd-ink);
    text-align: center;
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 1px var(--bd-line),
      0 30px 60px -30px rgb(58 45 42 / 0.55);
  }
  .welcome::backdrop {
    background: rgb(58 45 42 / 0.45);
    backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
  }
  .welcome-title {
    font-family: var(--bd-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 40px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--bd-accent-deep);
  }
  .welcome-lines {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 28px 0 30px;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .welcome-lines p {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--bd-ink-soft);
  }
  .glyph {
    flex: none;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: 13px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    font-size: 20px;
    background: var(--bd-accent-soft);
  }
  .welcome-foot {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .welcome-go {
    padding: 12px 26px;
    font-size: 16px;
  }
</style>
